@startuml lifecycle-usage
title warren/lifecycle — ordered start, readiness gate, reverse stop\nsource: lifecycle/SPEC.md (approved 2026-08-01); warren.md §2.3, §1.3

participant "adapters\n(pool, repos, consumers, servers)" as adapters
participant "Lifecycle" as lc
participant "readiness gate\n(read by warren/health)" as gate

adapters -> lc : Append(Hook{Name, OnStart,\nOnStop, Timeout})
note right : appended as singletons instantiate\nin topological order → registration\norder IS dependency order

[o-> lc : Start(ctx)  — boot step 6
lc -> adapters : OnStart: pool → repos →\nconsumers → servers
lc -> gate : step 7 — readiness opens
note right : a failing OnStart stops boot\nbefore readiness ever opens

[o-> lc : SIGTERM
lc -> gate : step 9 — readiness → 503 FIRST
note right : LB drains BEFORE anything stops —\nthe ordering hand-rolled services\nget backwards
[o-> lc : Stop(ctx)  — step 10
lc -> adapters : OnStop in exact reverse:\nservers → consumers →\nrelay flush → pools
note right : per-hook Timeout;\nforce-exit deadline (default 30s)\nbounds the whole shutdown
@enduml
